 "content": "# Continual ARC task notes: task-d06d6d7f

Solved one instance after two wrong submissions and one demonstration request. This task appears to be denoising structured monochrome shapes on a uniform background. Demonstration: 26x15 grid, background 6, foreground 1; anomalous single pixels with colors 3, 7, 9 occurred both inside and outside shapes. Output removes the anomalies: inside a 1-region restore 1; outside restore 6. Therefore do NOT globally replace noise with background; use shape continuity/context to restore underlying color.

Test example had background 4, foreground shapes in colors 1, 5, and 0; noise markers 2,7,8,9. Correct solution restored marker cells to their region's color or background and preserved the full structured regions. Notably noise can interrupt shape contours or appear as single cells adjacent to an object; infer its expected color from geometry/continuity. Correct final output was accepted. Avoid assuming every colored marker is noise without checking region layout. For this instance, first two candidate outputs were rejected because they failed to repair some in-object noise pixels (particularly 7/2 embedded in 1 shapes and 8/2 within 0-region shape)."
